        </div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>

  <p>
    If you are still early, decide which door realistically fits your timeline and budget: the MBA route if you
    can commit the time and cost for a shot at MBB and tier-2 strategy firms, or the direct-entry route into Big
    4 and boutique firms if you want to start sooner or want to test the fit before committing to further study.
    Either way, start structured case practice well ahead of placement season rather than a month before it.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      If you are unsure whether consulting genuinely fits how you like to work, or whether the MBA route is worth
      the cost for your situation, the
      <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/career-resources?topic=career-planning">career resources library</a>
      and <a href="/career-skills-compass/">Career &amp; Skills Compass</a> can help you compare it against other
      high-exposure career paths before you commit real prep time to it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    If you are choosing between the MBA route, direct entry, or a completely different path, or trying to work
    out whether your background and goals actually fit consulting's pace, a session with
    <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/">career guidance</a>
    can help you work through the decision with real numbers instead of guesswork, so you back the route that
    genuinely unlocks high-income opportunities for your profile instead of chasing a brand name. Or start with
    the free <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/assessments">career and skill assessments</a>
    if you are still unsure which direction genuinely fits how you like to work.
  </p>

